.TH SCS 1 "2026-11-11" "scs 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scs \- a very cool TUI clock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scs
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scs
displays a large pixel-font clock with a date, a minute progress bar, and
optional seconds. It supports animated glow, nine color themes, and a static
mode for scripts and screenshots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-static
Print one frame and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.IR PATH .
The default is
.IR ~/.config/scs/config.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-12h
Use 12-hour time.
.TP
.B \-\-24h
Use 24-hour time.
.TP
.B \-\-seconds
Show seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-seconds
Hide seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Enable ANSI colors.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Select a color theme. Valid names are neon, sunset, matrix, ice, candy, fire,
ocean, mono, and rainbow.
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " FPS"
Set the animation rate. Values are clamped to 10\-144.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q ", " Esc
Quit.
.TP
.B c
Cycle the color theme.
.TP
.B h
Toggle 12/24-hour time.
.TP
.B s
Toggle seconds.
.TP
.B r
Reset options to the values loaded at startup.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scs/config.toml
Default configuration file. If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set, the file is read from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/scs/config.toml .
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses simple
.I key = value
lines. Blank lines and text after
.B #
are ignored. Command-line options override configuration values.
.PP
Supported keys:
.TP
.B theme
Theme name as a quoted or unquoted string.
.TP
.B twelve_hour
Boolean. Use 12-hour time.
.TP
.B show_seconds
Boolean. Show seconds.
.TP
.B fps
Integer animation rate, clamped to 10\-144.
.TP
.B color
Boolean. Enable ANSI colors.
.PP
Example:
.nf
theme = "matrix"
twelve_hour = false
show_seconds = true
fps = 30
color = true
.fi
.SH THEMES
neon, sunset, matrix, ice, candy, fire, ocean, mono, and rainbow.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage or configuration.
